          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Recall that the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+product"} symmetric product
            (or symmetric power) of a space, say
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            points in
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            without considering the order in which they appear. Since repetitions are allowed, one has to think carefully as to how to deal with multiplicities: either to respect them or to ignore them. The first case, respecting multiplicities, means that
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,1,1\}
            and
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,0,1\}
            are not considered equivalent. The second means that they are.
          %p
            On this page we use the first definition, respecting multiplicities, and work with the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            %a{:href => "#MR0210096"} MR0210096
          %p
            There is a link between this space and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+group"} unitary group
            of a finite dimensional complex
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+matrix"} unitary matrix
            is determined completely by its
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenvalue"} eigenvalue
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiset"} bags
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The notion of the
            %em symmetric product
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            is an application of the construction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+power"} symmetric power
            in a symmetric monoidal category, where the category is
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Top
            and the monoidal structure is given by the cartesian product.
          #sympcircle.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a topological space. Let
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %strong
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                th symmetric product
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi SP
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(X)
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^n
              by the action of the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            On this page, we are most interested in the case
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = S^1
            but it will be instructive to consider also
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^*
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 \to \mathbb{C}^*
            and the exponential map
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_20.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \to S^1
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            The main property of
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi SP
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(S^1)
            is the following description, due to H. R. Morton in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#MR0210096"} MR0210096
          #symcirdesc.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The topological space
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(S^1)
              is a fibre bundle over
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
              with fibre an
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-1
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_25.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              is odd, the bundle is orientable; if
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_26.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              is even then it is not.
            %p
              In particular,
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_27.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^2(S^1)
              is a Möbius strip.
          %p
            Before proving this, let us give the descriptions of
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_28.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi SP
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(\mathbb{C}^*)
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_29.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(\mathbb{R})
          #symcplx.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The topological space
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_30.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(\mathbb{C}^*)
              is homeomorphic to
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_31.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^{(n-1)} \times \mathbb{C}^*
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The proof rests on giving an alternative description of
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_32.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(\mathbb{C}^*)
              in which the lack of ordering of the points is built in at the start. This description is given by taking the polynomial whose roots are the points (here we can see why it is important to take note of the multiplicities).
            %p
              We define a map
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_33.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi SP
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Poly
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(\mathbb{C}^*) \to \Poly_n
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_34.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_35.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi ζ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ζ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\zeta_1,\dots,\zeta_n]
              to the monic polynomial
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_36.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi ζ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi ζ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (z - \zeta_1)\cdots (z - \zeta_n)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
              onto its image. That image is the space of monic polynomials with non-zero constant term (as all the
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_37.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ζ
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \zeta_j
              are non-zero). There is an obvious homeomorphism of this space to
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_38.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^{n-1} \times \mathbb{C}^*
              given by taking coefficients.
          %p
            This space is relevant because the construction
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_39.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi SP
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(-)
            respects homotopy equivalences. Hence
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_40.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi SP
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(S^1)
            is homotopy equivalent to
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_41.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            and the map
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_42.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi SP
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(S^1) \to S^1
            is given by multiplying the
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_43.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            elements of a point in
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_44.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(S^1)
          #sphaus.num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              The space
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_45.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(S^1)
              is Hausdorff.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              It embeds in the Hausdorff space
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_46.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi SP
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(\mathbb{C}^*)
          #symreal.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The space
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_47.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(\mathbb{R})
              is homeomorphic to
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_48.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \times (\mathbb{R}_+)^{n-1}
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              The idea of this proof is that although in
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_49.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(\mathbb{R})
              an
              = succeed "-tuple" do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_50.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_51.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_52.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(\mathbb{R})
              has a unique representation as
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_53.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (t_1,t_2,\dots,t_n)
              where
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_54.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mi j
                      %mo ≤
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mrow
                          %mi j
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_j \le t_{j+1}
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_55.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(\mathbb{R}) \to \mathbb{R} \times (\mathbb{R}_+)^{n-1}
              by:
            .maruku-equation
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_56.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 2
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 3
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (t_1,t_2, \dots, t_n) \mapsto (t_1, t_2 - t_1, t_3 - t_2, \dots, t_n - t_{n-1}).
            %p
              There is another map which is worth mentioning. The space
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_57.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              has an invariant subspace under the action of the symmetric group (the
              = succeed "-fold" do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_58.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_59.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(\mathbb{R}) \to \mathbb{R} \times (\mathbb{R}_+)^{n-1}
              where the first map is the orthogonal projection onto this subspace. The projection is given by the map which sends
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_60.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{t_1,\dots,t_n\}
              to the average value. The fibre of this map is the quotient by the action of the symmetric group of the space of vectors in
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_61.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              whose components sum to zero. As they sum to zero, knowing the differences between the points (in the order imposed from
              = succeed ")" do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_62.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            .maruku-equation
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_63.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mi j
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mn 2
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (t_1,t_2,\dots,t_n) \mapsto \left(\frac{1}{n} \sum t_j, t_2 - t_1, \dots, t_n - t_{n-1}\right).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_of_proposition_
              Proof of Proposition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#symcirdesc"}
            %p
              Now let us prove the proposition. Guided by the description for
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_64.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi SP
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℂ
                        %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(\mathbb{C}^*)
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_65.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \colon SP^n(S^1) \to S^1
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_66.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi ζ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi ζ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi ζ
                        %mn 1
                      %mi …
                      %msub
                        %mi ζ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p(\{\zeta_1,\dots,\zeta_n\}) = \zeta_1 \dots \zeta_n
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_67.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \in S^1
              we define a map
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_68.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi λ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mover
                      %mi λ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mover
                      %mi λ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{-1}(\lambda) \times (S^1 \setminus \{\overline{\lambda}\}) \to p^{-1}(S^1 \setminus \{\overline{\lambda}\})
              by:
            .maruku-equation
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_69.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi ζ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ζ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ,
                    %mi λ
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi ζ
                      %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ζ
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    p(\{\zeta_1,\dots,\zeta_n\},\lambda e^{i t}) = \{\zeta_1 e^{i t/n}, \dots, \zeta_n e^{i t/n}\}
            %p
              where
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_70.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi π
                      %mo ,
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in (-\pi,\pi)
            %p
              It remains to determine the fibre at
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_71.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              and the gluing map at, say,
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_72.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -1
            %p
              To do this, we consider the exponential map
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_73.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi SP
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi SP
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(\mathbb{R}) \to SP^n(S^1)
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_74.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(\mathbb{R})
              as
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_75.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \times (\mathbb{R}_+)^{n-1})
              to view
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_76.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(\mathbb{R})
              as a bundle over
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_77.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_78.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(\mathbb{R}) \to SP^n(S^1)
              is a bundle map covering the exponential map
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_79.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R} \to S^1
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_80.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{R}_+)^{n-1} \to p^{-1}(1)
              given by the following recipe:
            %ol
              %li
                Start with
                = succeed "." do
                  %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_81.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi r
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi r
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi r
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mo +
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (r_1,r_2,\dots,r_{n-1}) \in (\mathbb{R}_+)^{n-1}
              %li
                Form the sequence of partial sums
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_82.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s_1,s_2,\dots,s_n)
                where
                = succeed "." do
                  %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_83.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mo &lt;
                            %mi k
                        %msub
                          %mi r
                          %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_k = \sum_{j \lt k} r_j
                = succeed "." do
                  %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_84.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mn 1
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_1 = 0
              %li
                Adjust so that their average (equivalently, sum) is
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_85.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                by setting
                = succeed "." do
                  %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_86.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi t
                          %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_k = s_k - \frac{1}{n} \sum s_j
              %li
                Apply the exponential function to produce
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_87.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mi π
                          %mi i
                          %msub
                            %mi t
                            %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{e^{2 \pi i t_k}\}
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_88.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi SP
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(S^1)
            %p
              To use this to identify the fibre of
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_89.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{-1}(1)
              we restrict this to a simplex. The simplex that we choose at the start is:
            .maruku-equation
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_90.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi n
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %msub
                      %mi r
                      %mi j
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta^n = \{(r_1,r_2,\dots,r_{n-1}) \in [0,1]^n : \sum r_j \le 1\}.
            %p At the second step, this becomes:
            .maruku-equation
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_91.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi n
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi j
                    %mo ≤
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{(s_1,s_2,\dots,s_n) \in [0,1]^n : s_j \le s_{j+1}\}.
            %p At the third step, this becomes:
            .maruku-equation
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_92.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≤
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{(t_1,t_2,\dots,t_n) \in \mathbb{R} : \sum t_j = 0,\; t_n \le t_1 + 1\}.
            %p Thus far, all the maps are by homeomorphisms of their ambient spaces and so are homeomorphisms as they are bijections.
            %p
              We now wish to determine the image of this in
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_93.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi SP
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(S^1)
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_94.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi ζ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ζ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\zeta_1,\dots,\zeta_n\}
              be a point in
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_95.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{-1}(1)
            %p
              Having chosen the first point, we now choose a preimage of that point in
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_96.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_97.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_1
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_98.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              using the same logarithm. If the chosen point had multiplicities and some are at the end of the list, then these are lifted consistently with having gone around the circle, which means that they are lifted to
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_99.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_1 + 1
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_100.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (t_1,t_2,\dots,t_n)
              with
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_101.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi j
                    %mo ≤
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_j \le t_{j+1}
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_102.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mi n
                      %mo ≤
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_n \le t_1 + 1
            %p
              To see that we can obtain any integer for the sum, consider what happens if we change our choice of first point to the next point anticlockwise. If our original point was multiple and there are others at the start of the list then this means that we shift one point to the end of the list. If we have moved to a new point and it is multiple, then we put all of its points at the start of the list and none at the end. When looking at what happens to the logarithm, we have shifted the cut around (possibly) and now lift starting at
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_103.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_2
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_104.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_1
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_105.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t_1 + 1
              = succeed "-tuple" do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_106.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_107.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mn 3
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi t
                        %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (t_2,t_3,\dots,t_n,t_1+1)
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_108.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              = succeed "-tuple" do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_109.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_110.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              which sum to
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_111.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_112.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{-1}(1)
            %p
              It is also injective. The above discussion shows that changing the choice of first point changes the sum by integral values and it is also clear that changing the starting point of the logarithm changes it by multiples of
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_113.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "." do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_114.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            %p
              As the simplex is compact and
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_115.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{-1}(1)
              is Hausdorff, the map
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_116.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n \to p^{-1}(1)
              is thus a homeomorphism.
            %p
              The last step is to identify the transition map. As we go around the circle, we need to adjust the above to take into account the variation in sum. This can be done at the last step where we map to
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_117.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi SP
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(S^1)
              by multiplying each term by
              = succeed "," do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_118.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi e
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mi π
                          %mi i
                          %mi τ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^{2 \pi i \tau/n}
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_119.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi π
                        %mi i
                        %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^{2 \pi i \tau}
              is the desired product of all the points. The effect that this has on the logarithm is, after a complete revolution, to add
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_120.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{n}
              to each component. This results in an
              = succeed "-tuple" do
                %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_121.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_122.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              so to correct that we have to move one term from the end to the beginning. This results in a coordinate transformation
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_123.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (t_1,t_2,\dots,t_n) \mapsto (t_n - 1, t_1, t_2, \dots, t_{n-1})
              which is orientable if
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_124.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              is odd and unorientable if
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_125.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              is even.
          %p
            Let us illustrate this for the case
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_126.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_127.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi SP
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^2(S^1)
            consists of equivalence classes of pairs of points
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_128.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi ζ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ζ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\zeta_1,\zeta_2\}
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_129.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_130.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            at
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_131.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            we have the condition
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_132.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ζ
                    %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi ζ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \zeta_1 \zeta_2 = 1
            and so we can write our pair as
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_133.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi ζ
                    %mo ,
                    %mover
                      %mi ζ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\zeta,\overline{\zeta}\}
          %p
            On the subset
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_134.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ζ
                  %mo ≠
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \zeta \ne -1
            there is a clear parametrisation with domain
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_135.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1)
            given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_136.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi π
                        %mi t
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi i
                        %mi π
                        %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \mapsto \{e^{i \pi t}, e^{-i \pi t}\}
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_137.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1] \to p^{-1}(1)
            by sending
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_138.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_139.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{-1,-1\}
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_140.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ζ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \zeta
            to
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_141.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℜ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ζ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Re(\zeta)
            and then composing with an appropriate inverse trigonometric function, but it is more instructive to consider why this works.
          %p
            Let us imagine that we approach
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_142.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{-1,-1\}
            and pass through it. Both before and after, we have two dots moving around the circle mirroring each other. At the crucial time, they meet at
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_143.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -1
          %p
            Hence the fibre at
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_144.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{-1}(1)
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_145.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]
          %p
            Now consider what happens as we move around the circle. Suppose that we look at a path on the boundary which starts at the image of
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_146.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            as we move around, then when we are at
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_147.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi π
                        %mi i
                        %mi t
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^{2 \pi i t} \in S^1
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_148.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mi π
                        %mi i
                        %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^{\pi i t}
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_149.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^{\pi i} = -1
            which is the image of
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_150.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %h2#conjugacy_classes_of_unitary_matrices Conjugacy Classes of Unitary Matrices
          %p
            The symmetric product
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_151.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi SP
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SP^n(S^1)
            can be identified with the space of conjugacy classes of unitary transformations on
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_152.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^n
            = succeed "-matrices." do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_153.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \times n
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_154.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_155.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi conj
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi SP
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_n/conj \simeq SP^n(S^1)
            and the induced map
            %math#mathml_fa175beab15f8569bed8296f8be965b806b28905_156.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_n \to S^1
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant"} determinant
            mapping.
